// Position 5 of main.kama's list: a module `static` named `type`, written and read in the file that
// declares it. It has a file of its own because a static is in scope throughout its file, and main.kama's
// parameter and local named `type` may not take a name in scope (a static cannot be exported, so the read
// reaches main.kama through a function).
export { typeStatic };

static int32 type = 100;

fn int32 typeStatic() { return type; }
